# Testing Guidelines

## Unit tests

- Framework: xUnit (`x-pad.Tests/`)
- SDK: Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk; coverlet.collector present
- Keep tests out of the WinExe project via `DefaultItemExcludes`

```bash
dotnet test
```

## What to cover

- Encoding / EOL / BOM round-trips (`FileService`)
- Session / recovery serialization edge cases
- Pure helpers (search, indent detection, keybinding catalog, sanitizers)
- Prefer focused unit tests over UI automation for ViewModels/services

## Patterns

- Descriptive names: `Method_Scenario_Expected`
- Independent tests; no shared mutable temp state without cleanup
- Use temp directories under the test run, not `%APPDATA%/XPad`

## Smoke (manual / script)

```powershell
pwsh scripts/smoke-cli.ps1
pwsh scripts/smoke-single-instance.ps1  # skips if xpad already running
pwsh scripts/smoke-workspace.ps1
```

Manual checklist (see `AGENTS.md`): tabs + dirty close, themes, find/replace, Open Folder, encoding re-decode, crash recovery, Open with.

## Requirements (hybrid)

- New logic in Services/Editor should ship with unit tests when practical
- Bug fixes should add a regression test when the failure is reproducible without the UI
- Do not require 80% UI coverage; prioritize encoding, session, and search correctness

---
**Hybrid:** existing xUnit + smoke scripts; stronger coverage on critical services
